# The site is served from the repo root, so repository housekeeping files
# end up publicly reachable alongside the pages. None of them contain
# anything sensitive, but they are not part of the website and an indexable
# site should not be offering Google a README to crawl.
#
# 301 to the homepage rather than 404, because these are not missing pages,
# they are files that simply have no business being a URL.

/wrangler.jsonc   /   301
/README.md        /   301
/.gitignore       /   301

# NOT HERE, and it was tried: rules turning /services.html into a 301.
# Workers' own html_handling normalisation runs BEFORE _redirects, so the
# platform answers those with a 307 and the rules never fire. Verified
# against the live site rather than assumed.
#
# Setting html_handling to "none" would hand them back to this file, but it
# would also stop /services resolving at all, and /services is now the
# canonical URL on every page and in the sitemap. The 307 stays.
#
# Practically it costs nothing: the only place those .html URLs ever
# existed was the github.io address, which is switched off, and Google has
# been told the real URLs by both canonical tag and sitemap.
